  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll read the project instructions and source-room details, then build a reproducible analysis and use its checked figures across the report, presentation, workbook, and JSON.",
    "I’m applying the installed OpenSocrates controller to the recommendation judgment and keeping its evidence limits explicit. I’ll now inspect the source dictionary and assumptions before deciding how to model the options.",
    "The exports contain repeated IDs, revisions, cancelled and test records, a future shipment, and zero-price shipments. I’m resolving the latest record per ID before applying eligibility rules, then I’ll quarantine any returns that cannot be linked to the eligible 2025 base.",
    "The base-case ranking favors Czechia plus Spain: about €198,099 annual incremental contribution on €225,000 capex and five FTE. Its modeled joint stress leaves only about €32,180 annually, so I’m comparing that exposure with the more resilient Netherlands plus Spain option before setting the board recommendation and release gates.",
    "The first document pass exposed a few prose figures that didn’t match the generated totals. I’m correcting those from the machine-checked country records, then I’ll validate the rendered PDFs and workbook structure before handing them over.",
    "The accounting, scenario, provenance, workbook, and PDF checks now pass. I’ve also inspected rasterized pages: the report is five pages, the board deck is seven slides, and the tables and charts render without visible clipping. I’m finishing the reproduction notes and the limitations log.",
    "The board package is complete. It recommends **staging Czechia and Spain** within **€225,000 capex and five FTE**. This pair has the highest modeled base annual increment, **€198,099**. Its joint-stress increment falls to **€32,180**, so the report gates Czechia’s capital release after a Spain pilot and compares **Netherlands plus Spain**, which retains **€107,630** under that stress.\n\n- [Executive report](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/executive_report.pdf)\n- [Board presentation](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/board_presentation.pdf)\n- [Analytical workbook](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/analytical_workbook.xlsx) and [metrics JSON](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/metrics.json)\n- [Reproduction instructions](<CELL>/workspace/README.md) and [source register](<CELL>/workspace/sources/source_register.json)\n\nVerification passed for monthly-to-country reconciliation, all 72 feasible scenario records, archived source hashes, workbook charts, and PDF text and page counts. I also inspected rendered pages for clipping. The material limit is that hub uplift and costs are synthetic scenario assumptions, not measured causal effects; the PDFs state the decision gates and omitted cash-flow items.\n\nOpenSocrates native application remains unverified by its runtime; the complete selected procedure was read and used.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3"
  ],
  "final": "The board package is complete. It recommends **staging Czechia and Spain** within **€225,000 capex and five FTE**. This pair has the highest modeled base annual increment, **€198,099**. Its joint-stress increment falls to **€32,180**, so the report gates Czechia’s capital release after a Spain pilot and compares **Netherlands plus Spain**, which retains **€107,630** under that stress.\n\n- [Executive report](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/executive_report.pdf)\n- [Board presentation](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/board_presentation.pdf)\n- [Analytical workbook](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/analytical_workbook.xlsx) and [metrics JSON](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/metrics.json)\n- [Reproduction instructions](<CELL>/workspace/README.md) and [source register](<CELL>/workspace/sources/source_register.json)\n\nVerification passed for monthly-to-country reconciliation, all 72 feasible scenario records, archived source hashes, workbook charts, and PDF text and page counts. I also inspected rendered pages for clipping. The material limit is that hub uplift and costs are synthetic scenario assumptions, not measured causal effects; the PDFs state the decision gates and omitted cash-flow items.\n\nOpenSocrates native application remains unverified by its runtime; the complete selected procedure was read and used.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3",
